# Secrets of this Worker. `scripts/setup-environment.ts` saves staging's Cloudflare API token and
# account id to .env, and checks `git check-ignore` before it writes. That check sees only the one
# name it writes: a copy made by hand under another suffix, such as .env.txt or .env.bak, is not
# matched by the root .gitignore's `.env` line, so `git add -A` would commit the token. The second
# rule below covers the whole family of names, so no copy of it can be staged.
.env
.env.*
